# Explore Unit-Affine Rerandomization

Composite modular arithmetic has a trap: a nonzero multiplier can still collapse information. This interactive path develops the correction—use a **unit**, a residue coprime to the modulus—and connects it to LWE hybrid reasoning. For background, see [Learning with Errors](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Learning_with_errors), [Euler's totient function](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler%27s_totient_function), and the [Chinese Remainder Theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_remainder_theorem).

## 1. Watch bijections and collisions

Choose $q,a,b$ and inspect every arrow $x\mapsto ax+b$. Unit multipliers produce a permutation; nonunits visibly merge inputs.

