Translation by $b$ is always invertible. Multiplication by $a$ is invertible precisely when $a$ has a modular inverse, equivalently when $\gcd(a,q)=1$. Hence $x\mapsto ax+b$ is bijective exactly for unit $a$.

{{algorithm:0}}
</details>

## 2. Count the safe multipliers

The safe multipliers are counted by Euler's totient $\varphi(q)$. Explore how their density varies with the arithmetic shape of $q$.

