A uniform proposal is accepted with probability $\varphi(q)/q$, so rejection sampling uses $q/\varphi(q)$ proposals on average. If $m$ and $n$ are coprime, a residue is a unit modulo $mn$ exactly when both components are units, and $\varphi(mn)=\varphi(m)\varphi(n)$.

{{algorithm:1}}
</details>

## 3. Preserve every average

A unit-affine map merely reorders residues. Therefore for every statistic $f$,

$$
\sum_x f(ax+b)=\sum_x f(x).
$$

This is the distribution-preservation mechanism needed before querying a decision procedure.

