<details><summary>Reveal why the identity is distributional</summary>

Apply the sum identity to indicator functions. Every event has the same probability before and after transformation, so a uniform residue stays uniform. The conclusion concerns all statistics, not merely the examples shown numerically.
</details>

## 4. Find where a hybrid gap survives

If $q$ contributions sum to at least $\delta$, one contribution is at least $\delta/q$. Adjust the gaps and see the guaranteed threshold.

